rible  what was it what was it called oh it was  some stupid  hippie dip [ __ ] so and and um  and we both looked at each other when  let's just hang out this this is never  going to work wow because his his voice  was very high and pristine my voice was  kind of you know low and rough and it  just it sounded horrible and little by  little you know I guess I guess I don't  know what you know he he went this way  and I went this way and we kind of  figured out a way of singing together  and what was the first song that you  could go holy [ __ ] you know this is  better than that recording we did at  Temple University this is so cool we had  we had you know the first album we did  was just a collection of stuff that  songs that I had songs that he had it  wasn't really conceived like a record  but we we got a contract so we made the  record for Atlantic Records and it was  really the second album The Abandoned  luncheonette where it really came  together  um and that's what she's gone she's gone  was on that sort of that album and that  that song was you know I call that the  perfect storm that's uh the perfect  creative storm but
 

